From 7f6441f0d0c8a17dec4ddc4778ce5b1603cd0abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:01:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/34] net80211: add roaming decision logic with tests

Add the decisions for roaming between the APs of an ESS as plain C
without kernel dependencies, so that they can be tested on the build
host:

- the signal of the current AP is smoothed (EWMA, one sample per
  100 ms, weight 1/8);
- background scans only while the smoothed signal is below the
  threshold, with a gap that doubles from 5 s up to 60 s while scans
  find nothing; a signal that falls since the last scan resets it;
- a switch only to an AP that is at least 8 units stronger in two
  scans in a row, and not within 30 s after the last switch;
- an AP below the lost threshold is practically gone: scan every 5 s
  regardless of the dwell time and take any stronger AP at once.

The tests cover the single decisions and simulate a station with
noisy signals: equal APs give no switch within an hour, walking from
one AP to the other gives exactly one switch, and a vanishing AP is
left within a few seconds. Run them with
src/tests/libs/compat/openbsd_wlan/roam_logic_test.py.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
